    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Solve $4\\cos x=\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cosec}x$ for $0^\\circ\\le x\\le360^\\circ$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=30^\\circ,60^\\circ,210^\\circ,240^\\circ$.",
      "worked": "Since $\\sin x\\ne0$, multiply by $\\sin x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}4\\sin x\\cos x&=\\sqrt{3}\\\\2\\sin2x&=\\sqrt{3}\\\\\\sin2x&=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\\\2x&=60^\\circ,120^\\circ,420^\\circ,480^\\circ\\\\x&=30^\\circ,60^\\circ,210^\\circ,240^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nAll four values satisfy the original equation.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
